<p data-start="1069" data-end="1163">The GOOD NEWS:<br>
Your design style is excellent already.<br data-start="1123" data-end="1126">
It only needs responsive adjustments.</p>
<p data-start="1165" data-end="1177">I’d rate it:</p>
<ul data-start="1179" data-end="1282">
<li data-start="1179" data-end="1201">
<p data-start="1181" data-end="1201">Desktop UI: <strong data-start="1193" data-end="1201">9/10</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1202" data-end="1244">
<p data-start="1204" data-end="1244">Mobile compatibility currently: <strong data-start="1236" data-end="1244">5/10</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1245" data-end="1282">
<p data-start="1247" data-end="1282">After responsive redesign: <strong data-start="1274" data-end="1282">9/10</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1284" data-end="1369">The best next step is:<br>
✅ Convert all pages into responsive layouts before continuing.</p>
<p data-start="1371" data-end="1464">Because if you redesign every page first, then later fix mobile, you’ll repeat a lot of work.</p>
<p data-start="1466" data-end="1486">So I recommend next:</p>
<ol data-start="1487" data-end="1582">
<li data-start="1487" data-end="1513">
<p data-start="1490" data-end="1513">Make Home.js responsive</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1514" data-end="1558">
<p data-start="1517" data-end="1558">Then redesign Login/Register responsively</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1559" data-end="1582">
<p data-start="1562" data-end="1582">Then Dashboard/Admin</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1584" data-end="1632">And I can <span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent group inline cursor-pointer align-baseline whitespace-nowrap" role="button" tabindex="0"><span class="inline-flex items-center overflow-hidden align-middle" aria-hidden="true" style="opacity: 1; width: 1.5rem;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" data-rtl-flip="" class="group-hover:entity-accent icon text-token-text-primary inline-block transition-transform duration-150 ease-out group-hover:translate-x-0.5"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-b2090418.svg#e04414" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span><span class="group-hover:entity-accent whitespace-normal">give you a FULL responsive Home.js version that works on</span></span>:</p>
