rmal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="83">You’re right to call that out.<br data-start="30" data-end="33">
A single random image URL will not magically show:</p>
<ul data-start="84" data-end="152">
<li data-start="84" data-end="98">
<p data-start="86" data-end="98">van delivery</p>
</li>
<li data-start="99" data-end="116">
<p data-start="101" data-end="116">parcel movement</p>
</li>
<li data-start="117" data-end="131">
<p data-start="119" data-end="131">tracking map</p>
</li>
<li data-start="132" data-end="152">
<p data-start="134" data-end="152">courier atmosphere</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="154" data-end="206">all together exactly like your reference screenshot.</p>
<p data-start="208" data-end="300">Your reference image is actually a custom designed composite background, not a normal photo.</p>
<p data-start="302" data-end="328">So the proper solution is:</p>
<ul data-start="330" data-end="416">
<li data-start="330" data-end="371">
<p data-start="332" data-end="371">use YOUR exact screenshot background<br>
